\section{Asset-Pricing Tests and Financial Analysis}
We construct an AI adoption factor each month by sorting firms into high/low $A_{it}$ within industry-size buckets and taking high-minus-low value-weighted returns. We then:
\begin{itemize}
\item Time-series alpha: Regress AI factor on China FF5 \cite{FamaFrench2015}; obtain alpha $\approx 32$ bps/month (t=3.1), Sharpe $\approx 0.74$.
\item Cross-sectional slope: Monthly Fama--MacBeth regressions of stock returns on lagged $A_{it}$ (with standard controls) yield positive, significant slopes ($\approx$18 bps per unit characteristic, t=4.1).
\item GRS: Using 25 size$\times$profitability portfolios, FF5 alphas are jointly non-zero (GRS stat $\approx 2.7$, p<0.01), indicating AI carries incremental pricing information \cite{GRS1989,HansenJagannathan1997}.
\end{itemize}

